        "URL": "https://cryptonews.com/news/best-crypto-to-buy-now-13-november-xrp-solana-bitcoin/",
        "BODY": "Bitcoin rocketed to a historic peak of $126,080 in early October, but the much-hyped “Uptober” rally was cut short after Trump’s tariff announcement on China triggered a sharp selloff on October 6, sparking a month-long correction across the market. For seasoned crypto investors, the pullback came as no surprise and was even seen as healthy. Market corrections often flush out excess leverage and speculative trading, paving the way for explosive rebounds. Now, as volatility cools and confidence begins to return, analysts expect momentum to rebuild heading into 2026. Here’s why XRP, Solana, and Bitcoin could emerge as major winners in the next bullish cycle. XRP (XRP): Powering the Future of Global Payments Ripple’s XRP ($XRP) continues to redefine international money transfers with its fast, low-cost blockchain payment network, aiming to replace legacy systems such as SWIFT. Ripple’s network has been highlighted in reports from the UN Capital Development Fund and the White House, while it continues forming strategic partnerships with top-tier financial institutions. This expansive reach has helped XRP become the fourth biggest crypto by market capitalization, currently around $150.8 billion. Ripple’s latest initiative, the RLUSD stablecoin, pegged to the U.S. dollar, underscores its strategy to get a foothold in what may be the biggest crypto use case. Every RLUSD transaction, along with other activity on the XRP Ledger, incurs a tiny XRP burn, directly linking token utility to network growth. Over the past year, XRP has soared 279%, hitting $3.65 in mid-July, its first new all-time high since 2018. In the same period, Bitcoin only grew 22% in price. XRP grew 2.6% in the last 24 hours, while Bitcoin dropped 2%. Its RSI of 60 indicates buying momentum is picking back up, signalling the likelihood of a recovery to $3 by late November. Should the U.S. greenlight spot crypto ETFs and pass Project Crypto (a reform proposal for clearer digital asset laws), XRP could realistically surpass $10 by early 2026. Solana (SOL): Ethereum’s Main Rival Eyes $1,000 Milestone Solana ($SOL) stands out as one of the most efficient and scalable blockchain ecosystems on the market. With a market cap of $86 billion and $10 billion in total value locked (TVL), Solana’s ecosystem is the second biggest layer 1 in DeFi after Ethereum. The recent approval of Grayscale and Bitwise Solana spot ETFs on the New York Stock Exchange has sparked optimism for a new wave of institutional inflows, similar to what fueled Bitcoin and Ethereum rallies in prior cycles. After bottoming near $100 earlier this year, Solana rebounded to around $156. A bullish flag formed across its support and resistance lines from mid-September to now, inviting the possibility of a spectacular breakout. Key support lies around $150, while resistance sits near $250. If ETF-driven demand accelerates, SOL could challenge its previous all-time high of $293.31, and in a bullish scenario, potentially rally past $450, with $1,000 as a long-term target during the next major cycle. Bitcoin (BTC): Could the King of Crypto Reach $250,000 by 2026? Bitcoin ($BTC) , the cornerstone of the digital asset industry, continues to dominate investor sentiment after notching its record $126,080 high on October 6. If U.S. regulators move forward with Project Crypto, a framework aimed at modernizing securities laws for digital assets, or if Trump’s proposed U.S. Strategic Bitcoin Reserve gains political traction, Bitcoin’s valuation could realistically reach $250,000 by 2026. Even without these catalysts, Bitcoin has set multiple new ATHs this year and could notch another near $150,000 this quarter. Touted as “digital gold”, Bitcoin believers point to its year-on-year growth to argue it is a hedge against inflation, drawing both retail and institutional capital. Currently, Bitcoin represents over $2 trillion of the global crypto market’s $3.57 trillion capitalization, solidifying its status as the anchor of the blockchain economy. Bitcoin Hyper (HYPER): A Meme Coin with Real Utility and Layer-2 Power One emerging contender for 2026’s spotlight is Bitcoin Hyper ($HYPER) , a project that blends meme culture with serious blockchain innovation. Unlike typical meme coins, HYPER serves a vital purpose as a Butcoin layer-2 scaling solution, designed to boost network throughput, lower fees, and enable smart contract functionality. Built using the Solana Virtual Machine (SVM), Bitcoin Hyper features DAO governance, cross-chain interoperability, and programmable contracts that allow seamless integration of Bitcoin across multiple networks. The project has already raised $27 million in presale funding, with analysts like Borch Crypto projecting up to 100× growth potential. A Coinsult audit verified that HYPER has no security vulnerabilities, enhancing investor trust. The HYPER token fuels the network, used for staking, governance, and transaction fees. Those who stake tokens during the presale can earn up to 43% APY through staking rewards. With Bitcoin nearing new highs and HYPER’s presale gaining strong traction, this could become one of the breakout success stories of 2026. Visit the official presale website or follow Bitcoin Hyper on X and Telegram for more information. Visit the Official Website Here The post Best Crypto to Buy Now 13 November – XRP, Solana, Bitcoin appeared first on Cryptonews .",
